```java
import java.util.Map;
import java.util.stream.Collectors;

public Car getMostPopularCar(List<Car> cars) {
    Map<String, Integer> carCountMap = cars.stream()
            .collect(Collectors.groupingBy(Car::getColor, Collectors.summingInt(Car::getCount)));

    return carCountMap.entrySet().stream()
            .max(Map.Entry.comparingByValue())
            .map(Map.Entry::getKey)
            .map(color -> new Car(color, ((Map.Entry<String, Integer>) carCountMap.entrySet().stream()
                    .max(Map.Entry.comparingByValue()).get()).getValue()))
            .orElse(null);
}
```

This method first groups the cars by their color and counts the number of each color. Then, it finds the color with the highest count and returns a new `Car` object with that color and the total count of cars with that color. If there are no cars in the list, it returns `null`.

